    "terrainName": "farm",
    "description": "What: a rider fires from horseback (CE-4623 AB-1 / AB-5; docs/designs/animals/DESIGN_Animals.md §5 / §9). On the farm terrain a 'War horse' (TKB 704, fearless) carries a 'Rider' (Friend, rifle) in its saddle — a firing seat (±150°) — and gallops east along y = 160 from x 0 to x 260 at 12 m/s, passing two men 25 m off its line ('Target 1', 'Target 2', Hostile, hold fire); nobody orders the rider to fire: a man in a firing seat engages on his own (CE-3454, FireFromSeat — his SOP's first row). Judge: (1) the horse gallops (over 8 m/s) (2) the rider fires from the saddle (3) a target is hit (4) the war horse never bolts under fire (5) the rider is still in the saddle at the end. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh ua-animal-horse-rider"
  },
